      <trans-unit id="fpa-intro-title" datatype="html">
        <source>Introduction to Function Point Analysis</source>
        <context-group purpose="location">
          <context context-type="sourcefile">src/app/components/home/home.component.html</context>
          <context context-type="linenumber">28,31</context>
        </context-group>
      </trans-unit>
      <trans-unit id="fpa-intro" datatype="html">
        <source> Function Point Analysis (FPA) is a software measurement technique that quantifies the functionality provided to the end user based on a requirements specification. It is used to estimate the size, effort, and cost of software development. Here is an overview of the method: </source>
        <context-group purpose="location">
          <context context-type="sourcefile">src/app/components/home/home.component.html</context>
          <context context-type="linenumber">32,34</context>
        </context-group>
      </trans-unit>
      <trans-unit id="fpa-steps" datatype="html">
        <source>Steps of Function Point Analysis</source>
        <context-group purpose="location">
          <context context-type="sourcefile">src/app/components/home/home.component.html</context>
          <context context-type="linenumber">37,40</context>
        </context-group>
      </trans-unit>
      <trans-unit id="steps1" datatype="html">
        <source>Identification of System Boundaries:</source>
        <context-group purpose="location">
          <context context-type="sourcefile">src/app/components/home/home.component.html</context>
          <context context-type="linenumber">40,41</context>
        </context-group>
      </trans-unit>
      <trans-unit id="step1-desc" datatype="html">
        <source>Define the boundaries of the system to be measured. The boundary separates the system from the external environment.</source>
        <context-group purpose="location">
          <context context-type="sourcefile">src/app/components/home/home.component.html</context>
          <context context-type="linenumber">42,43</context>
        </context-group>
      </trans-unit>
      <trans-unit id="step2" datatype="html">
        <source>Counting Data Functions:</source>
        <context-group purpose="location">
          <context context-type="sourcefile">src/app/components/home/home.component.html</context>
          <context context-type="linenumber">45,46</context>
        </context-group>
      </trans-unit>
      <trans-unit id="step2-ilf" datatype="html">
        <source><x id="START_BOLD_TEXT" ctype="x-b" equiv-text="&lt;b&gt;"/>Internal Logical Files (ILF)<x id="CLOSE_BOLD_TEXT" ctype="x-b" equiv-text="&lt;/b&gt;"/>: Sets of data or information that are maintained within the system.</source>
        <context-group purpose="location">
          <context context-type="sourcefile">src/app/components/home/home.component.html</context>
          <context context-type="linenumber">47,48</context>
        </context-group>
      </trans-unit>
      <trans-unit id="step2-eif" datatype="html">
        <source><x id="START_BOLD_TEXT" ctype="x-b" equiv-text="&lt;b&gt;"/>External Interface Files (EIF)<x id="CLOSE_BOLD_TEXT" ctype="x-b" equiv-text="&lt;/b&gt;"/>: Sets of data or information that are maintained outside the system but are used by the system.</source>
        <context-group purpose="location">
          <context context-type="sourcefile">src/app/components/home/home.component.html</context>
          <context context-type="linenumber">49,50</context>
        </context-group>
      </trans-unit>
      <trans-unit id="step3" datatype="html">
        <source>Counting Transactional Functions:</source>
        <context-group purpose="location">
          <context context-type="sourcefile">src/app/components/home/home.component.html</context>
          <context context-type="linenumber">52,53</context>
        </context-group>
      </trans-unit>
      <trans-unit id="step3-ei" datatype="html">
        <source><x id="START_BOLD_TEXT" ctype="x-b" equiv-text="&lt;b&gt;"/>External Inputs (EI)<x id="CLOSE_BOLD_TEXT" ctype="x-b" equiv-text="&lt;/b&gt;"/>: Processes that receive data or information from the user.</source>
        <context-group purpose="location">
          <context context-type="sourcefile">src/app/components/home/home.component.html</context>
          <context context-type="linenumber">54,55</context>
        </context-group>
      </trans-unit>
      <trans-unit id="step3-eo" datatype="html">
        <source><x id="START_BOLD_TEXT" ctype="x-b" equiv-text="&lt;b&gt;"/>External Outputs (EO)<x id="CLOSE_BOLD_TEXT" ctype="x-b" equiv-text="&lt;/b&gt;"/>: Processes that send data or information to the user.</source>
        <context-group purpose="location">
          <context context-type="sourcefile">src/app/components/home/home.component.html</context>
          <context context-type="linenumber">55,56</context>
        </context-group>
      </trans-unit>
      <trans-unit id="step3-eq" datatype="html">
        <source><x id="START_BOLD_TEXT" ctype="x-b" equiv-text="&lt;b&gt;"/>External Inquiries (EQ)<x id="CLOSE_BOLD_TEXT" ctype="x-b" equiv-text="&lt;/b&gt;"/>: Processes that involve querying data or information by the user. </source>
        <context-group purpose="location">
          <context context-type="sourcefile">src/app/components/home/home.component.html</context>
          <context context-type="linenumber">56,57</context>
        </context-group>
      </trans-unit>
      <trans-unit id="step4" datatype="html">
        <source>Assigning Weights to Functions</source>
        <context-group purpose="location">
          <context context-type="sourcefile">src/app/components/home/home.component.html</context>
          <context context-type="linenumber">59,60</context>
        </context-group>
      </trans-unit>
      <trans-unit id="step4-desc" datatype="html">
        <source>Each type of function (ILF, EIF, EI, EO, EQ) is assigned a weight based on complexity (Low, Medium, High).</source>
        <context-group purpose="location">
          <context context-type="sourcefile">src/app/components/home/home.component.html</context>
          <context context-type="linenumber">61,62</context>
        </context-group>
      </trans-unit>
      <trans-unit id="step5" datatype="html">
        <source>Calculating Unadjusted Function Points (UFP)</source>
        <context-group purpose="location">
          <context context-type="sourcefile">src/app/components/home/home.component.html</context>
          <context context-type="linenumber">64,65</context>
        </context-group>
      </trans-unit>
      <trans-unit id="step5-desc" datatype="html">
        <source>Multiply the quantity of each type of function by its respective weight and sum the results. </source>
        <context-group purpose="location">
          <context context-type="sourcefile">src/app/components/home/home.component.html</context>
          <context context-type="linenumber">66,68</context>
        </context-group>
      </trans-unit>
      <trans-unit id="step5-note" datatype="html">
        <source><x id="START_ITALIC_TEXT" ctype="x-i" equiv-text="&lt;i&gt;"/>This step is performed automatically by the system.<x id="CLOSE_ITALIC_TEXT" ctype="x-i" equiv-text="&lt;/i&gt;"/></source>
        <context-group purpose="location">
          <context context-type="sourcefile">src/app/components/home/home.component.html</context>
          <context context-type="linenumber">68,69</context>
        </context-group>
      </trans-unit>
      <trans-unit id="step6" datatype="html">
        <source>Adjusting Function Points</source>
        <context-group purpose="location">
          <context context-type="sourcefile">src/app/components/home/home.component.html</context>
          <context context-type="linenumber">70,71</context>
        </context-group>
      </trans-unit>
      <trans-unit id="step6-desc" datatype="html">
        <source>Apply adjustment factors based on general characteristics of the system, such as performance, security, etc. This results in the Adjusted Function Points (AFP).</source>
        <context-group purpose="location">
          <context context-type="sourcefile">src/app/components/home/home.component.html</context>
          <context context-type="linenumber">72,73</context>
        </context-group>
      </trans-unit>
      <trans-unit id="step6-note" datatype="html">
        <source><x id="START_ITALIC_TEXT" ctype="x-i" equiv-text="&lt;i&gt;"/>The adjustments are recalculated automatically by the system.<x id="CLOSE_ITALIC_TEXT" ctype="x-i" equiv-text="&lt;/i&gt;"/></source>
        <context-group purpose="location">
          <context context-type="sourcefile">src/app/components/home/home.component.html</context>
          <context context-type="linenumber">74,75</context>
        </context-group>
      </trans-unit>
      <trans-unit id="formula" datatype="html">
        <source>Formula</source>
        <context-group purpose="location">
          <context context-type="sourcefile">src/app/components/home/home.component.html</context>
          <context context-type="linenumber">78,80</context>
        </context-group>
      </trans-unit>
      <trans-unit id="afp-formula" datatype="html">
        <source>AFP = UFP x [0.65 + (0.01 x Σ(Adjustment Factors))]</source>
        <context-group purpose="location">
          <context context-type="sourcefile">src/app/components/home/home.component.html</context>
          <context context-type="linenumber">81,83</context>
        </context-group>
      </trans-unit>
      <trans-unit id="formula-desc" datatype="html">
        <source>Where:</source>
        <context-group purpose="location">
          <context context-type="sourcefile">src/app/components/home/home.component.html</context>
          <context context-type="linenumber">83,86</context>
        </context-group>
      </trans-unit>
      <trans-unit id="afp" datatype="html">
        <source><x id="START_BOLD_TEXT" ctype="x-b" equiv-text="&lt;b&gt;"/>AFP (Adjusted Function Points)<x id="CLOSE_BOLD_TEXT" ctype="x-b" equiv-text="&lt;/b&gt;"/>: final value that represents the adjusted measure of the software&apos;s functionality, taking into account various complexity factors.</source>
        <context-group purpose="location">
          <context context-type="sourcefile">src/app/components/home/home.component.html</context>
          <context context-type="linenumber">86,87</context>
        </context-group>
      </trans-unit>
      <trans-unit id="ufp" datatype="html">
        <source><x id="START_BOLD_TEXT" ctype="x-b" equiv-text="&lt;b&gt;"/>UFP (Unadjusted Function Points)<x id="CLOSE_BOLD_TEXT" ctype="x-b" equiv-text="&lt;/b&gt;"/>: initial measure of the software&apos;s functionality, calculated based on the number and complexity of data and transactional functions without any adjustments.</source>
        <context-group purpose="location">
          <context context-type="sourcefile">src/app/components/home/home.component.html</context>
          <context context-type="linenumber">88,90</context>
        </context-group>
      </trans-unit>
      <trans-unit id="adjustment-factors" datatype="html">
        <source><x id="START_BOLD_TEXT" ctype="x-b" equiv-text="&lt;b&gt;"/>Σ(Adjustment Factors)<x id="CLOSE_BOLD_TEXT" ctype="x-b" equiv-text="&lt;/b&gt;"/>: the sum of all adjustment factors that account for various characteristics of the system, such as performance, security, and other attributes that affect its complexity.</source>
        <context-group purpose="location">
          <context context-type="sourcefile">src/app/components/home/home.component.html</context>
          <context context-type="linenumber">91,93</context>
        </context-group>
      </trans-unit>
      <trans-unit id="constant-factor" datatype="html">
        <source><x id="START_BOLD_TEXT" ctype="x-b" equiv-text="&lt;b&gt;"/>0.65<x id="CLOSE_BOLD_TEXT" ctype="x-b" equiv-text="&lt;/b&gt;"/>: constant factor that represents a baseline level of complexity for the software system.</source>
        <context-group purpose="location">
          <context context-type="sourcefile">src/app/components/home/home.component.html</context>
          <context context-type="linenumber">94,95</context>
        </context-group>
      </trans-unit>
      <trans-unit id="conversion-factor" datatype="html">
        <source><x id="START_BOLD_TEXT" ctype="x-b" equiv-text="&lt;b&gt;"/>0.01<x id="CLOSE_BOLD_TEXT" ctype="x-b" equiv-text="&lt;/b&gt;"/>: a conversion factor that converts the adjustment factors from percentage points to a decimal form.</source>
        <context-group purpose="location">
          <context context-type="sourcefile">src/app/components/home/home.component.html</context>
          <context context-type="linenumber">96,97</context>
        </context-group>
      </trans-unit>
      <trans-unit id="formula-explanation" datatype="html">
        <source> The formula for calculating Adjusted Function Points (AFP) takes into account the Unadjusted Function Points (UFP) and adjusts them based on various factors that affect the system&apos;s complexity and performance. The constant factor 0.65 represents a baseline level of complexity, while the sum of the adjustment factors, multiplied by 0.01, accounts for additional complexities. This adjustment ensures that the final AFP value accurately reflects the overall functionality and complexity of the software system. </source>
        <context-group purpose="location">
          <context context-type="sourcefile">src/app/components/home/home.component.html</context>
          <context context-type="linenumber">102,106</context>
        </context-group>
      </trans-unit>
      <trans-unit id="benefits" datatype="html">
        <source>Benefits of FPA</source>
        <context-group purpose="location">
          <context context-type="sourcefile">src/app/components/home/home.component.html</context>
          <context context-type="linenumber">110,113</context>
        </context-group>
      </trans-unit>
      <trans-unit id="benefit1" datatype="html">
        <source><x id="START_BOLD_TEXT" ctype="x-b" equiv-text="&lt;b&gt;"/>Accurate Estimates<x id="CLOSE_BOLD_TEXT" ctype="x-b" equiv-text="&lt;/b&gt;"/>: Helps provide more accurate estimates of effort and cost.</source>
        <context-group purpose="location">
          <context context-type="sourcefile">src/app/components/home/home.component.html</context>
          <context context-type="linenumber">113,114</context>
        </context-group>
      </trans-unit>
      <trans-unit id="benefit2" datatype="html">
        <source><x id="START_BOLD_TEXT" ctype="x-b" equiv-text="&lt;b&gt;"/>Project Comparison<x id="CLOSE_BOLD_TEXT" ctype="x-b" equiv-text="&lt;/b&gt;"/>: Allows comparison of different software projects.</source>
        <context-group purpose="location">
          <context context-type="sourcefile">src/app/components/home/home.component.html</context>
          <context context-type="linenumber">114,115</context>
        </context-group>
      </trans-unit>
      <trans-unit id="benefit3" datatype="html">
        <source><x id="START_BOLD_TEXT" ctype="x-b" equiv-text="&lt;b&gt;"/>Productivity Measurement<x id="CLOSE_BOLD_TEXT" ctype="x-b" equiv-text="&lt;/b&gt;"/>: Facilitates the measurement of the development team&apos;s productivity. </source>
        <context-group purpose="location">
          <context context-type="sourcefile">src/app/components/home/home.component.html</context>
          <context context-type="linenumber">115,117</context>
        </context-group>
      </trans-unit>
      <trans-unit id="benefit4" datatype="html">
        <source><x id="START_BOLD_TEXT" ctype="x-b" equiv-text="&lt;b&gt;"/>Resource Planning<x id="CLOSE_BOLD_TEXT" ctype="x-b" equiv-text="&lt;/b&gt;"/>: Helps plan resources and schedules for software projects.</source>
        <context-group purpose="location">
          <context context-type="sourcefile">src/app/components/home/home.component.html</context>
          <context context-type="linenumber">117,118</context>
        </context-group>
      </trans-unit>
      <trans-unit id="fpa-summary" datatype="html">
        <source> Function Point Analysis is a standardized and widely used technique in the software industry to measure the functionality and complexity of software systems. </source>
        <context-group purpose="location">
          <context context-type="sourcefile">src/app/components/home/home.component.html</context>
          <context context-type="linenumber">121,123</context>
        </context-group>
      </trans-unit>
    </body>
